What is the number of chloride ions produced when the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` (tetraamminedichloroplatinum(IV) chloride) is dissolved in an aqueous solution?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
When the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` is dissolved in an water, it dissociates into its ions. The compound is a positive cations and two individual chlorine anions. Thus, the dissociation equation is:
\[ [Pt(NH_3)_4Cl_2][Cl_2] \rightarrow [Pt(NH_3)_4Cl_2]^{2+} + 2 \text{Cl}^- \]
