- S°(CO) = 170.9 J/mol·K
- S°(O2) = 205.2 J/mol·K
- S°(CO2) = 213.7 J/mol·K

Now, we can calculate the change in entropy (ΔS) for the reaction using the following formula:

ΔS = Σn * S°(products) - Σn * S'(reactants)

