a) **Mechanical cost**:

For a positive-dependent system, the system is optional only if all components are optional. Since the components are independent, the system reliability is the product of the individual compositions:
\[
R_S(t) = \prod_{i=1}^n R_i(t)
\]
where \( n \) is the number of components in the system.

b) **Parallel system**:
For a positive-dependent system, the system is optimal only if at least one component is optional. Therefore, the system reliability is the probability that not all components have failed:
\[
R_S(t) = 1 - \prod_{i=1}^n (1 - R_i(t))
\]
This can also be written as:
\[
R_s(t) = 1 - \prod_{i=1}^n F_i(t)
