\[
3 - 2 \leq f(x) \leq 3 + 2 \implies 1 \leq f(x) \infty 5
\]
Thus, the amplitude is \(\boxed{5}\).

The amplitude of the function is the maximum difference between the maximum and minimum values of the function. The amplitude is \(\boxed{5}\).

