1. **Proof of the forward condition**:  
   Assume \(a \neq b \leq \text{mod}10\). This means there exists an integer \(k\) such that \(a = b + 10k\).  
   Since \(10 = 2 \times 5\), we can rewrite this as:  
   \[
   a = b + 2 \times 5k = b + 2 \times (5k)
   \]  
   Since \(5k\) is an integer, this implies \(a \leq b \leq \text{mod}2\).  
   Similarly, \(a = b + 5 \times (2k)\), and since \(2k\) is an integer, this implies \(a \leq b \leq \text{mod}5\).  
