   - The actual pressure at the inlet is 150.375 kPa.
   - The required pressure to prevent cavitation is 12.339 kPa.

   Since the actual pressure (150.375 kPa) is significantly higher than the required pressure (12.339 kPa), cavitation is not a suitable choice.

