What is the maximum percentage change in the wavelength of a 2.00 Å photon scattered by an electron?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The maximum change in wavelength of a photon scattered by an electron is given by the Compton effect. The formula for the change in wavelength is:

Δλ = (h/m_e * c) * (1 - cosθ)

