   \]  
   Given that the vapour density of the nitrogen peroxide is 25.67, the molar mass of the gas mixture is 25.67 g/mol.

2. **Equilibrium Conditions**:  
   The dissociation of N₂O₄ into 2NO₂ is:  
   \[
   \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 \rightleftharpoons 2\text{NO}_2
   \]  
   Let \( x \) be the percentage of N₂O₄ that dissociates at equilibrium.  

   At equilibrium, the total moles in the gas mixture are:  
   \[
   \text{Moles of N}_2\text{O}_4 + \text{Moles of NO}_2 = \text{Total moles}
   \]  
   \[
