","(a) The force on the proton is given by \(F = qE\), where \(q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}\) and \(E = 500 \, \text{N/C}\).  
\[
F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}
\]
Using Newton's second law, \(F = ma\), we find the acceleration:
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2
\]

(b) The formula for velocity as a function of time, assuming initial velocity is zero, is \(v = at\). We are given \(v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s}\) and we calculated \(a = 4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2\). Solving for \(t\):
\[
t = \frac{v}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 7.32 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{s}
\]

Final Answer: \(\boxed{7.32 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{s}}\)",fluency,"# Task Description
