","To determine the increase in the total entropy of the combined system, we can use the formula for entropy change in an adiabatic process:

\[
\Delta S = \Delta S_{\text{gas}} + \Delta S_{\text{water}}
\]

For the gas, the entropy change is:

\[
\Delta S_{\text{gas}} = m_g c_p \ln \left( \frac{T_2}{T_1} \right)
\]

For the water, the entropy change is:

\[
\Delta S_{\text{water}} = \Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{Q_{\text{water}}}{T_{\text{water}}}
\]

Given that all the heat transferred from the gases goes to the water, the heat lost by the gases is equal to the heat added to the water:

\[
Q_{\text{water}} = -Q_{\text{gas}}
