   \]  
   \[
   2567 = 9200 - 92x + 92x
   \]  
   This seems incorrect, the original answer was incorrect.  

   The correct answer is:  
   \[
   \text{Average molar mass} = \frac{(100 - x)(92) + (2x)(46)}{100} = 25.67
   \]  
   \[
   (100 - x)(92) + 2x(46) = 25.67 \times 100 = 2567
   \]  
   \[
   9200 - 92x + 92x = 2567
   \]  
