- \( n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3 \).

The refractive indices of GaAs and Ga\(_{0.2}\)Al_{0.8}\)As are:
- \( n_{\text{Ga}} \approx 3.36 \) at \( \lambda = 1 \, \mu \text{m} \).
- \( n_{\text{GaAl}} \approx 3.1 \) at \( \lambda = 1 \, \mu \text{m} \).

Assuming \( n_c = n_{\text{Ga}} = 3.36 \) and \( n_f = n_{\text{GaAl}} = 3.1 \), we can calculate the decay length:
\[
n_c - n_f = 3.36 - 3.1 = 0.26
\]
However, the reference gives \( n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \approx 0.3 \), so we can use this to find \( n_{\text{eff}} \):
\[
n_{\text{eff}} = n_f + 0.3 = 3.1 + 0.3 = 3.4
\]
Thus, the refractive index of the core is \( n_c = 3.4 \).

Now, we can calculate the decay length:
\[
\boxed{l = \frac{\lambda}{2\pi} \sqrt{\frac{1}{n_c^2 - n_f^2}}} = \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{2\pi} \sqrt{\frac{1}{3.4^2 - 3.1^2}} = \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{2\pi} \sqrt{\frac{1}{11.56 - 9.61}} = \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{2\pi} \sqrt{\frac{1}{1.95}}
\]
\[
\boxed{l \approx \frac{1 \times 10^{-6}}{2\pi} \times 0.707 = 3.57 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{m}}
\]
\[
\boxed{l \approx 357 \, \text{nm}}
\]

